         * Contract/oracle:
         * SinFunction is the real library function sin(x), which is 2*pi periodic. Therefore,
         * solving the same bracketing problem after shifting min/max/initial by 2*pi must shift
         * the computed root by 2*pi as well. A throw-deleting or seed-special-casing patch can
         * suppress the known NPE yet still return an inconsistent result on nearby valid inputs.
         */
        double tol = Math.max(new BisectionSolver().getAbsoluteAccuracy(), 1.0e-12) * 8.0 + 1.0e-12;
