             * Contract/oracle:
             * From the documented/tested behavior of BooleanUtils.toBoolean(String), the only
             * 3-character token accepted as true is case-insensitive "yes"; every other
             * 3-character string must parse as false. This catches throw-deleting patches that
             * return an incorrect boolean instead of crashing.
             */
            if (s != null && s.length() == 3 && !equalsIgnoreAsciiCase(s, "yes")) {
                if (result) {
                    throw new RuntimeException(
                        "[oracle:false-3char] metamorphic violation: non-yes 3-char token must parse as false input="
                            + repr(s) + " lhs=" + result + " rhs=false");
                }
